# Gate C-4's decisive real-time case: a schedule whose deadline passes
# while the process is closed is recovered -- delivered, not merely
# reconciled -- once the app reopens. `sleep` is a genuine wall-clock
# sleep in the *test harness*, not the guest; pairing it with the
# smallest duration this app's own command surface can create (10s,
# via a single add-10s) keeps this test's real runtime bounded rather
# than requiring a virtual clock this repo does not have.
#
# `restart` tears the process down and reopens it exactly like a real
# closed-then-reopened app would: the durable schedule's real deadline
# has already passed by the time this runs, so reconciliation queues
# an elapsed delivery, and mounting delivers it -- the same host
# behavior Gate C-4 restored (see ../FINDINGS.md, TIMER-F002/F007).

mount
activate add-10s
key enter
expect text mode "Mode: running"
expect countdown countdown

sleep 10500
restart

expect text mode "Mode: elapsed"
expect text sessions "Sessions: 1"
expect text countdown "00:00"
